  "contentBlockIcons": {
    "_comment": "A SECOND, deliberately separate dialect. opencatalogi's page editor (PageContentForm.vue `iconOptions`) offers exactly these names for ContentBlocks cards, they are stored in page/register data, and the PUBLIC Softwarecatalogus website renders them with its own glyph set. They are documented for end users in Softwarecatalogus website/docs/Handleidingen/pagina-beheer.md, so they are a published contract \u2014 renaming them to MDI would break the public site and invalidate that documentation. They are governed here rather than exempted: any lowercase icon value MUST be one of these, so a typo or a stray kebab-case MDI name is caught.",
    "_owner": "opencatalogi src/modals/pageContents/PageContentForm.vue (iconOptions)",
